      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Comparing the rate of semantic shift for \"sovereignty\" to \"governance\" and \"agency\" to \"functionality\" in digital text corpora vs. traditional linguistic evolution might involve:\n\n1. Longer-term linguistic and semantic trend studies\n2. Methodologically robust corpus sampling and segmentation\n3. Frequency or co-occurrence comparisons between preserved and shed words\n\nHowever, you might find support in similarities between accelerated semantic shifts in digital text with other potentially analogous changes, such as explosion rates of 'natural language processing', deep learning, or use of precise vies tensions across recent numerical outstanding linguistic observations during site explosive events.",
